{#- smp-report-schema: 1 -#}
{#- Python owns CI policy, check classification and symbolic link selection;
    this template owns presentation. -#}
{#- Keep blank lines around details blocks so GitHub renders their Markdown. -#}

{#- # Display logic -#}
{%- set job = report.job -%}
{%- set start_ms = job.metrics_query_start * 1000 -%}
{%- set end_ms = job.metrics_query_end * 1000 -%}
{%- set filter_start = (job.metrics_query_start - 7200) * 1000 -%}
{%- set filter_end = (job.metrics_query_end + 3600) * 1000 -%}
{%- set goals = report.experiments | selectattr("optimization_goal.result")
    | sort(attribute="optimization_goal.result.percent_change", reverse=true) | list -%}
{%- set changes = goals | rejectattr("erratic")
    | selectattr("optimization_goal.result.is_significant_change") | list -%}
{#- Orange heading when the section holds any regression, green otherwise. -#}
{%- set change_symbol = "🟠" if (changes | rejectattr("optimization_goal.result.is_improvement") | list) else "🟢" -%}
{%- set other_goals = namespace(rows=[]) -%}
{%- for exp in goals -%}
{%- if exp not in changes -%}
{%- set other_goals.rows = other_goals.rows + [exp] -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- set missing = report.experiments | selectattr("optimization_goal")
    | rejectattr("optimization_goal.result") | map(attribute="name") | sort | list -%}
{%- set no_goals = report.experiments | rejectattr("optimization_goal")
    | map(attribute="name") | sort | list -%}
{%- set crashed = report.failed_replicates | selectattr("replicate_type", "equalto", "non_profiling")
    | selectattr("is_dead") | map(attribute="experiment") | unique | sort | list -%}
{%- set retried = report.failed_replicates | selectattr("replicate_type", "equalto", "non_profiling")
    | rejectattr("is_dead") | map(attribute="experiment") | unique | sort | list -%}

{#- Report links configuration. -#}
{#- URL templates -#}
{%- macro metrics_dashboard_link() -%}
[Metrics dashboard](https://app.datadoghq.com/dashboard/ykh-ua8-vcu/SMP-Regression-Detector-Metrics?fromUser=true&refresh_mode=paused&tpl_var_run-id%5B0%5D={{ job.id }}&view=spans&from_ts={{ start_ms }}&to_ts={{ end_ms }}&live=false)
{%- endmacro -%}
{%- macro profiles_link() -%}
[Target profiles](https://app.datadoghq.com/profiling/explorer?query=env%3Asingle-machine-performance%20service%3Adatadog-agent%20job_id%3A{{ job.id }}&agg_m=count&agg_m_source=base&agg_t=count&fromUser=false&viz=stream&start={{ filter_start }}&end={{ filter_end }}&paused=true)
{%- endmacro -%}
{%- macro logs_link(name) -%}
[Logs](https://app.datadoghq.com/logs?query=experiment%3A{{ name | urlencode }}%20job_id%3A{{ job.id }}&agg_m=count&agg_m_source=base&agg_q=%40span.url&agg_q_source=base&agg_t=count&fromUser=true&index=single-machine-performance-target-logs&messageDisplay=inline&refresh_mode=paused&storage=hot&stream_sort=time%2Cdesc&top_n=100&top_o=top&viz=stream&x_missing=true&from_ts={{ filter_start }}&to_ts={{ filter_end }}&live=false)
{%- endmacro -%}
{%- macro bounds_dashboard_link(name) -%}
[bounds checks dashboard](https://app.datadoghq.com/dashboard/vz3-jd5-bdi?fromUser=true&refresh_mode=paused&tpl_var_experiment%5B0%5D={{ name | urlencode }}&tpl_var_job_id%5B0%5D={{ job.id }}&view=spans&from_ts={{ start_ms }}&to_ts={{ end_ms }}&live=false)
{%- endmacro -%}
{%- macro debug_dashboard_link(rep) -%}
[Debug Dashboard](https://app.datadoghq.com/dashboard/zv5-qgi-m66/smp-failed-replicates?fromUser=true&refresh_mode=paused&tpl_var_experiment%5B0%5D={{ rep.experiment | urlencode }}&tpl_var_job_id%5B0%5D={{ job.id }}&tpl_var_replicate_type%5B0%5D={{ rep.replicate_type }}&tpl_var_variant%5B0%5D={{ rep.variant }}&from_ts={{ filter_start }}&to_ts={{ filter_end }}&live=false)
{%- endmacro -%}
{#- Dispatching logic: for a given item, take the list of link names generated on the python side, map it to real URLs -#}
{%- macro header_link(template_name) -%}
{%- if template_name == "metrics_dashboard" -%}{{ metrics_dashboard_link() }}
{%- elif template_name == "profiles" -%}{{ profiles_link() }}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro -%}
{%- macro experiment_links(name, templates) -%}
{%- for template_name in templates -%}
{%- if not loop.first %} {% endif -%}
{%- if template_name == "logs" -%}{{ logs_link(name) }}
{%- elif template_name == "bounds_dashboard" -%}{{ bounds_dashboard_link(name) }}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- endmacro -%}
{%- macro default_experiment_links(name) -%}
{{ experiment_links(name, extra.links.experiments[name].default) }}
{%- endmacro -%}
{%- macro debug_link(rep) -%}
{%- for template_name in extra.links.failed_replicates -%}
{%- if not loop.first %} {% endif -%}
{%- if template_name == "debug_dashboard" -%}{{ debug_dashboard_link(rep) }}{% endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- endmacro -%}

{#- Tables -#}
{#- Tables retain the measurements needed to interpret each row. -#}
{%- macro delta_cell(exp) -%}
{{ "%+.2f" | format(exp.optimization_goal.result.percent_change) }}
{%- endmacro -%}
{%- macro goal_status(exp) -%}
{%- if exp.erratic -%}🔇
{%- elif exp.optimization_goal.result.is_significant_change -%}
{{ "🟢" if exp.optimization_goal.result.is_improvement else "🟠" }}
{%- else -%}➖
{%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro -%}
{%- macro goal_name(exp) -%}
{{ exp.name }}{{ " **(ignored)**" if exp.erratic else (" **(erratic)**" if exp.optimization_goal.result.is_erratic else "") }}
{%- endmacro -%}
{%- macro optimization_links(exp) -%}
{{ experiment_links(exp.name, extra.links.experiments[exp.name].optimization_goal) }}
{%- endmacro -%}
{%- macro check_links(c) -%}
{{ experiment_links(c.experiment, extra.links.experiments[c.experiment].checks[c.check_name]) }}
{%- endmacro -%}
{%- macro goal_table(rows) -%}
{{ rows | table([
  ["status", goal_status],
  ["experiment", goal_name],
  ["goal", "optimization_goal.goal", "format_goal_label"],
  ["Δ mean %", delta_cell],
  ["Δ mean % CI", "optimization_goal.result.confidence_interval", "format_confidence_interval"],
  ["links", optimization_links],
]) }}
{%- endmacro -%}
{#- Status symbols are fixed per category, so each table passes its own macro. -#}
{%- macro passed_status(c) -%}
{{- "info" if c.is_quantile else "✅" -}}
{%- endmacro -%}
{%- macro failed_gate_status(c) -%}❌{%- endmacro -%}
{%- macro failed_other_status(c) -%}🟠{%- endmacro -%}
{%- macro check_table(rows, status) -%}
{{ rows | table([
  ["status", status],
  ["experiment", "experiment"],
  ["check", "", "check_format_name"],
  ["replicates", "", "check_format_replicates_passed"],
  ["observed", "", "check_format_observed_value"],
  ["links", check_links],
]) }}
{%- endmacro -%}

{#- # Report content -#}

{#- ## Header -#}
**CI: {{ "✅ Passed" if extra.verdict.passed else "❌ Failed" }}.** {{ extra.verdict.summary }}

<details><summary>Run infos</summary>

**Run:** `{{ job.id }}`

**Baseline:** `{{ job.baseline_sha }}` | **Comparison:** `{{ job.comparison_sha }}`{% if shas_are_shas(job.baseline_sha, job.comparison_sha) %} | [diff](https://github.com/DataDog/datadog-agent/compare/{{ job.baseline_sha }}...{{ job.comparison_sha }}){% endif %}
{% for template_name in extra.links.header %}{{ " | " if not loop.first }}{{ header_link(template_name) }}{% endfor %}

</details>
{#- ## Diagnostics -#}
{%- if extra.verdict.missing_analysis %}

💥 **Error: missing optimization-goal analysis** for {{ extra.verdict.missing_analysis | join(", ") }}. This may be a result of misconfiguration. Ping [#single-machine-performance](https://dd.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C03LY8MQ73R) and we can help out.
{%- endif %}
{%- if missing | length > extra.verdict.missing_analysis | length %}

⚠️ **Missing or malformed optimization-goal data (non-blocking)** for {% for name in missing if name not in extra.verdict.missing_analysis %}{{ ", " if not loop.first }}{{ name }}{% endfor %}: no usable data was produced by the listed experiments.
{%- endif %}
{%- if crashed %}

⚠️ **Missing analysis due to target crashes** for {{ crashed | join(", ") }}: one or more replicates failed with a non-zero exit code. No optimization-goal or bounds-check analysis will be present for these experiments.
{%- endif %}
{%- if retried %}

⚠️ **Retried target crashes (non-blocking)** for {{ retried | join(", ") }}: one or more replicates failed and may have been retried.
{%- endif %}
{%- if report.analysis_errors %}

⚠️ **Analysis errors:** {% for e in report.analysis_errors %}{{ e.experiment }} ({{ e.check_name }}): {{ e.message }}{{ "; " if not loop.last }}{% endfor %}.
{%- endif %}
{#- ## Quality gates -#}
{%- if extra.check_categories.gates_failed %}

### ❌ Failed quality-gate bounds checks ({{ extra.check_categories.gates_failed | length }}, blocking)

{{ check_table(extra.check_categories.gates_failed, failed_gate_status) | trim }}
{%- endif %}
{%- if extra.check_categories.gates_passed %}

<details><summary>Passing quality-gate bounds checks ({{ extra.check_categories.gates_passed | length }})</summary>

{{ check_table(extra.check_categories.gates_passed, passed_status) | trim }}

</details>
{%- endif %}
{%- if extra.check_categories.other_failed %}

### 🟠 Other failed bounds checks ({{ extra.check_categories.other_failed | length }})

{{ check_table(extra.check_categories.other_failed, failed_other_status) | trim }}
{%- endif %}
{%- if extra.check_categories.other_passed or extra.check_categories.quantiles %}

<details><summary>Other checks: {{ extra.check_categories.other_passed | length }} passing bounds checks, {{ extra.check_categories.quantiles | length }} quantile measurements</summary>

{{ check_table(extra.check_categories.other_passed + extra.check_categories.quantiles, passed_status) | trim }}

</details>
{%- endif %}
{#- ## Optimization goals -#}
{%- if changes %}

### {{ change_symbol }} Significant performance changes ({{ changes | length }})

{{ goal_table(changes) | trim }}
{%- endif %}
{%- if other_goals.rows %}

<details><summary>Other optimization results ({{ other_goals.rows | length }})</summary>

{{ goal_table(other_goals.rows) | trim }}

</details>
{%- endif %}
{%- if no_goals %}

<details><summary>Experiments with no optimization goal ({{ no_goals | length }})</summary>

These experiments do not run change-detection analysis.

{{ no_goals | table([["experiment", ""], ["links", default_experiment_links]]) | trim }}

</details>
{%- endif %}
{#- ## Failed replicates -#}
{%- if report.failed_replicates %}

<details><summary>Replicate execution failures ({{ report.failed_replicates | length }} groups)</summary>

Target crashes can be retried up to 8 times. Dead non-profiling replicates prevent analysis for the experiment. Profiling replicates may still be executing; use the debug dashboard for current status.

{{ report.failed_replicates | table([
  ["experiment", "experiment"],
  ["variant", "variant"],
  ["type", "replicate_type"],
  ["replicates", "replicates", "format_replicate_buckets"],
  ["failure", "failure", "format_replicate_failure"],
  ["dead", "is_dead"],
  ["debug", debug_link],
]) | trim }}

</details>
{%- endif %}

{#- ## Methodology #}

<details><summary>Explanation</summary>

**CI policy:** bounds checks on `quality_gate_*` experiments are blocking. Job will fail
- if a check fails on one or more comparison replicate
- if blocking analysis failures are detected; they'll be flagged with 💥

Non-blocking analysis issues are indicated by ⚠️ and still deserve to be investigated.
Other bounds checks and optimization regressions do not fail CI.

**Optimization goals:** a change is significant when its absolute mean change is at least {{ job.tolerances.effect_size | format_percent }} and its {{ job.tolerances.p_value | pvalue_to_confidence | format_percent }} confidence interval excludes zero.
Meaning of status icons:
- 🟢 improvement,
- 🟠 regression,
- ➖ no significant change,
- 🔇 marked `erratic: true` in the experiment config. Such experiments are excluded from regression detection.

Note: The **(erratic)** tag marks high sample dispersion detected at runtime. Those results still count.

Ping [#single-machine-performance](https://dd.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C03LY8MQ73R) for help interpreting a report.

</details>
